# Correctness overlay for #516, authorized by the #429 patch policy.
# https://github.com/avalonalex/patina/issues/516
# Admit exact-width word lines; preserve explicit newlines and stream character
# chunks without adding a final newline. Keep cursor movement within the input
# when tokenizing words and grouping digits.
# Both Patina backends and Chibi reproduce the wrapping failures; Gauche also
# rejects out-of-range cursor movement tolerated by their integer cursors.
# The smoke driver enforces those boundaries for two maintained CI regressions.
# Reference staging renames library identities, selects portable optional-arg
# macros, and supplies SRFI 165 with vector-collected defaults to avoid Gauche's
# multiple-value limit. SRFI 166 implementation files are otherwise identical.
--- a/srfi/166/column.scm
+++ b/srfi/166/column.scm
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
